                <pb facs="0271" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1244: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant to the Special Representative of the
                        President</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ocheltree</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-21T13:00:00-06:00">June 21, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 27, June 14, 6 p.m., the President of
                    the Commission received telegrams this morning from the Governments of Honduras
                    and Nicaragua agreeing to the extension of article No. III of the pact December
                    10, 1937. Honduras accepted for a further period of 6 months; Nicaragua accepted
                    without <pb facs="0272" n="263" xml:id="pg263"/> time limit. This information
                    will be released to local press probably today.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ocheltree</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
